      "description": "A reading that does not exist is said in words at 17px, never as a number.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-tile\" tabindex=\"0\"><h2 class=\"ds-label\"><svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"4\" y=\"4\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"/><path d=\"M15 2v2M15 20v2M2 15h2M2 9h2M20 15h2M20 9h2M9 2v2M9 20v2\"/></svg>CPU</h2><div class=\"ds-figure ds-missing\">Unknown</div><p class=\"ds-caption\">No live reading · history below</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-tile{width:200px;height:168px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:16px 18px;border-radius:22px;background:var(--w-tile,#1d1f21);color:var(--w-text,#f2f2f7);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text','Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;overflow:hidden;transition:background-color .6s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)}.ds-label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;margin:0;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--w-text-2,#aeaeb2)}.ds-figure{margin-top:auto;font-family:ui-rounded,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Rounded',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:44px;font-weight:600;line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.02em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-unit{margin-left:3px;font-size:20px;letter-spacing:0;color:var(--w-text-2,#aeaeb2)}.ds-caption{margin:4px 0 0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35;color:var(--w-text-2,#aeaeb2);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-tile:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--w-blue-fill,#0a84ff);outline-offset:2px}.ds-missing{font-family:inherit;font-size:17px;letter-spacing:0;color:var(--w-text-2,#aeaeb2)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Disk Ring",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "tile",
      "description": "Large-tile disk ring: state fill on the track, percentage at the centre; label takes the accent colour.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-tile ds-large\" tabindex=\"0\"><h2 class=\"ds-label ds-accent-warn\"><svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M22 12H2\"/><path d=\"M5.45 5.11 2 12v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-6l-3.45-6.89A2 2 0 0 0 16.76 4H7.24a2 2 0 0 0-1.79 1.11z\"/><path d=\"M6 16h.01M10 16h.01\"/></svg>Disk</h2><div class=\"ds-ringrow\"><div class=\"ds-ring\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 128 128\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"64\" r=\"52\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--w-track,#2c2e31)\" stroke-width=\"14\"/><circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"64\" r=\"52\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--w-amber-fill,#ff9f0a)\" stroke-width=\"14\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"294 327\"/></svg><span>90%</span></div><div><div class=\"ds-figure ds-f40\">23.2<span class=\"ds-unit\">GB free</span></div><p class=\"ds-caption\">205 GB of 228 GB used</p></div></div></section>",
      "css": ".ds-tile{width:200px;height:168px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:16px 18px;border-radius:22px;background:var(--w-tile,#1d1f21);color:var(--w-text,#f2f2f7);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text','Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;overflow:hidden;transition:background-color .6s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)}.ds-label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;margin:0;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--w-text-2,#aeaeb2)}.ds-figure{margin-top:auto;font-family:ui-rounded,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Rounded',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:44px;font-weight:600;line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.02em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-unit{margin-left:3px;font-size:20px;letter-spacing:0;color:var(--w-text-2,#aeaeb2)}.ds-caption{margin:4px 0 0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35;color:var(--w-text-2,#aeaeb2);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-tile:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--w-blue-fill,#0a84ff);outline-offset:2px}.ds-large{width:416px;height:352px}.ds-accent-warn{color:var(--w-amber,#ffb340)}.ds-ringrow{flex:1;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px}.ds-ring{position:relative;width:136px;height:136px;flex-shrink:0}.ds-ring svg{width:100%;height:100%;transform:rotate(-90deg)}.ds-ring span{position:absolute;inset:0;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:30px;font-weight:600;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-f40{font-size:40px;margin-top:0}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Chart Tooltip",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "tooltip",
      "description": "Readout above a focused or hovered bar or sparkline point; solid Pop, no shadow.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-tip\"><strong>Mon 20 Oct</strong><br>14 files · 3.1 MB<br>9 new, 5 already on the NAS</div>",
      "css": ".ds-tip{display:inline-block;padding:6px 9px;border-radius:10px;background:var(--w-pop,#3a3c3f);color:var(--w-pop-text,#f2f2f7);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.3;white-space:nowrap}.ds-tip strong{font-weight:600}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Day Bars",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "tile",
      "description": "Files per day: muted green bars, today in healthy green, empty days as a track stub; each bar focusable.",
      "html": "<ol class=\"ds-bars\" aria-label=\"Files backed up per day\"><li tabindex=\"0\" style=\"height:40%\"></li><li tabindex=\"0\" class=\"ds-empty\"></li><li tabindex=\"0\" style=\"height:65%\"></li><li tabindex=\"0\" style=\"height:25%\"></li><li tabindex=\"0\" style=\"height:80%\"></li><li tabindex=\"0\" class=\"ds-today\" style=\"height:100%\"></li></ol>",
      "css": ".ds-bars{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;gap:3px;height:120px;width:200px;margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none}.ds-bars li{flex:1;border-radius:3px;background:var(--w-green-soft,#2b5236);outline:none}.ds-bars li:hover,.ds-bars li:focus-visible{background:var(--w-green-fill,#34c759);opacity:.75}.ds-bars li:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--w-blue-fill,#0a84ff);outline-offset:2px}.ds-bars .ds-today{background:var(--w-green-fill,#34c759)}.ds-bars .ds-empty{height:2px;background:var(--w-track,#2c2e31)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Device Row",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "tile",
      "description": "List row inside a tile; a late device turns its time and caption amber instead of gaining a badge.",
      "html": "<ul class=\"ds-list\"><li><div><div class=\"ds-t\">Harsh's Mac</div><div class=\"ds-c\">25 files · 5.7 MB</div></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><div class=\"ds-t\">Yesterday 23:03</div><div class=\"ds-c\">Last backup</div></div></li><li class=\"ds-late\"><div><div class=\"ds-t\">Mom's iPhone</div><div class=\"ds-c\">40 files · 7.7 MB</div></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><div class=\"ds-t\">11 Oct</div><div class=\"ds-c\">9 days ago</div></div></li></ul>",
      "css": ".ds-list{width:340px;margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--w-text,#f2f2f7)}.ds-list li{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;padding:10px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--w-rule,rgba(255,255,255,.08))}.ds-list li:last-child{border-bottom:0}.ds-t{font-size:15px;font-weight:600;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-c{font-size:13px;line-height:1.35;color:var(--w-text-2,#aeaeb2)}.ds-r{text-align:right}.ds-late .ds-r .ds-t,.ds-late .ds-r .ds-c{color:var(--w-amber,#ffb340)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Text Link",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "text-link",
      "description": "The world's only button form: a semibold blue text action.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-link\">Show older uploads</button>",
      "css": ".ds-link{background:none;border:0;padding:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--w-link,#4aa3ff);cursor:pointer}.ds-link:hover{opacity:.8}.ds-link:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--w-blue-fill,#0a84ff);outline-offset:2px;border-radius:6px}.ds-link:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:default}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Glance Widgets",
    "overview": "The NAS is read like a stack of Apple home-screen widgets. Each raised tile answers one question with one large rounded figure that can be read from across the room, a short label above it and a quiet caption below. Detail (exact values, history, per-device numbers) waits behind a hover, focus or tap; it never sits in the way of the figure.\n\nThe world is quiet greyscale on a near-black ground (a light grey ground in the light theme). Colour is not decoration and not category: it says healthy, needs attention or critical, and nothing else. When something is wrong, the place that reports it changes as a whole, the way a widget does, rather than collecting badges.\n\nThe system currently covers the dashboard at `/` and the disk indicator in the sidebar. Library, Finder, Search, Trash, Settings and Sync still render in the incumbent \"Liquid Glass\" shell (translucent blurred panels, Apple Blue accent, `--glass-*` and `--accent*` tokens in `globals.css`), sitting on this world's shared ground. They are the next surfaces to move over; until then the shell's tokens remain in force for them and are not part of this world.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Raised flat tiles in three sizes on a plain ground; no borders, no shadows, no blur.",
      "One big tabular figure per tile, in the system's rounded face.",
      "Colour for state only: green, amber, red; everything else greyscale.",
      "Exactly one tile (Needs attention) changes its whole background with state.",
      "Missing data is said in words, at a size that cannot pass for a number.",
      "System fonts only; nothing loads from the internet."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The State-Only Rule",
        "body": "Green, amber and red mean healthy, attention and critical. Categories, series and kinds are told apart in greys (the vault bar is text, Grey 1, Grey 2), never in hues.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Grey Line Rule",
        "body": "Sparklines are drawn in Grey 1 with a soft fade beneath. A metric earns state colour only when it has a threshold; temperature stays grey until the NAS's real sensor range is known.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every number that updates (figures, captions, times, sizes) uses tabular numerals so live values do not jitter.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Words-Not-Zeros Rule",
        "body": "A reading that does not exist is said in words (\"Unknown\", \"No data yet\", \"Not measured on this machine\") at the statement size in secondary text, never as a placeholder number.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Stack Rule",
        "body": "Tiles never take shadows, borders or backdrop blur. Separation comes from the step between ground and tile, nothing else.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do give each tile one question and one figure, with the figure at the tile's bottom edge.",
      "Do keep sparklines grey and the vault breakdown in greys; spend green, amber and red only on state.",
      "Do let Needs attention, and only Needs attention, change its whole background (Amber Tile, Red Tile).",
      "Do report state on other tiles through the label (`accent`) and their own marks (the ring, a late device's time).",
      "Do say missing readings in words at 17px in secondary text.",
      "Do use tabular numerals for every live number.",
      "Do keep blue for focus and links only."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add shadows, borders or backdrop blur to tiles.",
      "Don't give a second tile a whole-background state change; that move belongs to Needs attention.",
      "Don't add badges, pills or dots to signal a problem; change the tile, the label or the value's colour.",
      "Don't colour categories or data series with hues.",
      "Don't load fonts from the internet; use the system stack and ui-rounded.",
      "Don't show a placeholder or estimated number where no reading exists.",
      "Don't carry the Liquid Glass shell's glass panels, accent gradients, glows or uppercase tracked section labels into surfaces built in this world."
    ]
  }
}
